From b1274ff4f9266c35e2e1146a8a2c18eae264c528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:04:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-5 remaining seven data planes

Add the remaining seven batch-5 Units on top of the 19-layer source-lock
tree. No guest evidence is recorded; host catalog keeps all seven planned,
and the three new frameworks are deliberately minimal with explicit
catalog blockers.

- pahub-v20 (U040-B): CONTROL_PAHUB at 0x70 implementing the direct 1-byte
  PCA9548A channel mask (driver read-modify-write) only. Downstream bus
  forwarding/nesting is NOT modeled because the attachment framework is
  single-bus; 0x70 conflicts with env-iii.
- rtc (U126): US_RTC8563 at 0x51 with the BCD calendar register file
  (0x00/0x01 control, 0x02..0x08 seconds..year, 0x09..0x0F alarm/timer
  storage). The model advances seconds from the QEMU virtual clock when
  running and exposes a unix-time fixture; crystal/backup/alarm IRQ physics
  are NOT modeled and 0x51 conflicts with the ameter EEPROM.
- tmos-pir (U185): US_STHS34PF80 at 0x5A with WHOAMI 0xD3, CTRL/page
  register file and synthetic tobject/tambient/presence/motion/shock data
  registers; IR optics and thermal physics are NOT modeled and 0x5A
  conflicts with ncir/ncir2.
- neohex (A045-B): 37x WS2812C RMT capture on the yellow data line. The
  public UIFlow2 tree has no unit/neohex.py driver, so this is an explicit
  driver-gap model anchored on the generic neopixel path; LED optics/power
  and cascade limits are NOT modeled.
- lora-e220-433 (U170-433): UART responder with the 0xC0 write-config echo,
  0xC1 read-config mirror (8-byte config fixture) and idle-time fixture
  responses for other frames. RF/433MHz/air-rate/mode switching are NOT
  modeled and the page-115200-vs-driver-9600 conflict stays unresolved.
- zigbee (U110): UART responder that captures guest frames and injects
  deterministic ;-separated fixture responses after an idle gap; DRF1609H
  frame parsing is deliberately minimal and Zigbee mesh/RF/encryption are
  NOT modeled.
- nbiot2 (U111-B): UART AT responder using the same idle-time fixture
  mechanism; SIM7028 AT/MQTT/HTTP sequences are NOT decoded and cellular
  network/SIM/operator behavior is NOT modeled.
  The three UART Units share the existing TX-capture/RX-injection path and
  remain mutually exclusive on PORT.C.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest firmware) validates property
registration, fixtures, range/read-only rejection, the 37-LED shape and the
responder fixtures; it is not a functional PASS.
